The Earthly Book of Hours (earthlyhours.com)
Copyright © 2026 Ryan Weberling. All rights reserved.

Except as listed below, everything in this repository is the copyright of
Ryan Weberling: the writing (including the Lectio Terra posts), the
selection, arrangement, tagging and description of readings, images and
sources, the data files, the site's design, the Earthly Star glyph
(fonts/earthly-star), the postcards, and the code (including worker/).

This repository is public so that the site can be served from it, and the
site is meant to be read and shared.

You're welcome to, without asking:

- share screenshots or photos of the site, the readings or the postcards,
  on social media or anywhere else, ideally with a link to
  earthlyhours.com;
- quote short passages with credit;
- link to any page;
- print pages for personal, devotional or classroom use.

Please ask first (hello@earthlyhours.com) before copying the site or its
writing in bulk, republishing it, using it commercially or in an app or
platform, or using it to train AI systems. Beyond the uses above and what
GitHub's Terms of Service allow (viewing and forking on GitHub), no part
of this repository may be copied, republished, adapted or redistributed
without written permission.

Not covered by this notice, and keeping their own terms:

- Works in the public domain that the site quotes or reproduces, such as
  historical texts, plates, drawings and photographs. They remain in the
  public domain. The Sources page gives each work and its rights statement.
- Images, texts or scans credited to another person or institution, which
  keep that person's or institution's terms.
- The typefaces in fonts/ other than fonts/earthly-star: IM Fell English,
  Fraunces and Cormorant Garamond under the SIL Open Font License (OFL.txt
  in each folder), and GL-Morris under Gutenberg Labo's licence
  (fonts/gl-morris/LICENSE.txt).
- Software the site or the worker loads from elsewhere, such as the DFOS
  client libraries, under its own licence.
